Based on the linker errors, it appears the DAC emulator driver is not being compiled and linked into the final application. This would explain both the missing device symbols (`__device_dts_ord_...`) and the undefined reference to the driver function `dac_emul_value_get`.

The Zephyr build system enables and builds drivers based on the `compatible` properties found in the device tree. Looking at the provided overlay file `tests/drivers/dac/dac_emul/boards/native_sim.overlay`, the device node with the label `dac_emul0` is missing its `compatible` property.

Without a `compatible` property, the build system does not know which driver to associate with this device tree node. While other nodes have the correct property, this error in one of the nodes can be sufficient to prevent the driver from being correctly configured and built, leading to the observed linker errors for all related devices and functions.

The fix is to add the missing `compatible = "zephyr,dac-emul";` property to the `dac_emul0` node in the overlay file.

