Based on the provided source code and error log, there is an inconsistency in the naming of the DAC emulator driver across the project files. The error during the device tree processing stage indicates that the `compatible` property in the device tree overlay is not recognized by the build system.

The `prj.conf` file enables `CONFIG_DAC_EMUL`, and `src/main.c` includes `zephyr/drivers/dac/dac_emul.h`. These correspond to an older version of the driver, which uses the compatible string `"zephyr,dac-emul"`.

However, the `native_sim.overlay` file uses `compatible = "zephyr,dac-emulator";`. This is a newer compatible string used after the driver was renamed. This mismatch causes the device tree compiler to fail because it cannot find a binding for `"zephyr,dac-emulator"`.

The fix is to make the overlay file consistent with the rest of the project by using the older compatible string, `"zephyr,dac-emul"`.

